    {
      "source_number": "115",
      "group": "复习题",
      "source_pages": ["p0054#3"],
      "status": "ORIGINAL_MATH_SUPPORT_COMPLETE",
      "source_method_expectation": "Give any two solutions of each equation; full parametric sets below make the real radical domain and completeness explicit.",
      "parts": [
        {
          "part": "а",
          "original_conditions": ["sqrt(x)-sqrt(y)=1"],
          "domain": "x>=0,y>=0 in R; the equation further forces x>=1 and x>y.",
          "method": [
            "Set t=sqrt(y)>=0. Then sqrt(x)=t+1, so y=t^2 and x=(t+1)^2.",
            "Choose t=0 and t=1 to obtain (1,0) and (4,1)."
          ],
          "parametric_solution_set": {"x": "(t+1)^2", "y": "t^2", "parameter_domain": "t >= 0"},
          "requested_two_solutions": [["1", "0"], ["4", "1"]],
          "completeness_argument": "Every real solution determines t=sqrt(y)>=0 and therefore this unique form. Conversely, for each t>=0, principal roots are sqrt((t+1)^2)=t+1 and sqrt(t^2)=t, whose difference is 1. No extraneous squaring roots are introduced.",
          "limitations": []
        },
        {
          "part": "б",
          "original_conditions": ["sqrt(x+y)-sqrt(y)=1"],
          "domain": "y>=0 and x+y>=0 in R; the equation additionally forces x>=1.",
          "method": [
            "Set t=sqrt(y)>=0. Then sqrt(x+y)=t+1, so x+y=(t+1)^2 and x=2*t+1, y=t^2.",
            "Choose t=0 and t=1 to obtain (1,0) and (3,1)."
          ],
          "parametric_solution_set": {"x": "2*t+1", "y": "t^2", "parameter_domain": "t >= 0"},
          "requested_two_solutions": [["1", "0"], ["3", "1"]],
          "completeness_argument": "Every solution gives t=sqrt(y)>=0 and the displayed form. Conversely x+y=t^2+2*t+1=(t+1)^2, so the principal-root difference is (t+1)-t=1 for all t>=0. The original domain requires x+y>=0, not initially x>=0; x>=1 follows from solving.",
          "limitations": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "source_number": "116",
      "group": "复习题",
